{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound","id":1419250,"title":"So... Prometheus Unbound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-20T15:35:02-07:00","id":1419250,"title":"So... Prometheus Unbound","content":"I know it's going to be focused on the orders, with more information on psionics and how to use it, along with some technological goodies. But has anyone had a more in depth preview or commentary on what else will be in it? I mean, this isn't a &quot;Sell me&quot; because everything on the new Trinity line is on my &quot;must buy&quot; list, but I'd sort of like to hear more about it to distract me from the stressful stuff going on in the real world right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T15:45:51-07:00","id":1419253,"title":"","content":"More detail about the eight orders, how they work, their cultures, who\u2019s who, allies and foes, Paths and Edges, a chapter on psi powers, and technology used by each of them.<br /> <br /> What would you like to know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-20-2020, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T16:35:03-07:00","id":1419260,"title":"","content":"So I know I'm not the thread starter but I would like to give an answer to the question. <br /> <br /> Everything! <br /> <br /> hehe<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I have to admit that while all the above looks fascinating for me the Paths and Edges, and psi powers section look the most interesting. <br /> <br /> Of course, like the OP, I consider everything on the Trinity line as a &quot;must buy&quot; so 'most interesting' is like having it be a 12 and the rest be a 10 or 11. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T17:50:44-07:00","id":1419271,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans, either in Prometheus Unbound or beyond, to provide optional powers for different levels of modes? Example: If I'm not a fan of the Algesis 2 from the core, will there be an optional set of mode powers provided in any supplement? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T18:03:24-07:00","id":1419273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastion Avalos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419271#post1419271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans, either in Prometheus Unbound or beyond, to provide optional powers for different levels of modes? Example: If I'm not a fan of the Algesis 2 from the core, will there be an optional set of mode powers provided in any supplement?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah, that'd be something I'd be very interested in. I know that the original freeform system from the old players guide was seen to be clunky and had balance problems, but something that did give your characters a few more choices when choosing dots in a power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T18:07:53-07:00","id":1419275,"title":"","content":"Different powers for Mode levels? No. A system to let you manifest your own power options at different Mode levels (that isn\u2019t clunky like the old Player\u2019s Guide)? Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T18:38:21-07:00","id":1419278,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, is that a statement of what you'd consider desirable or something under active development for Prometheus Unbound or another future supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T18:53:20-07:00","id":1419279,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I wasn\u2019t clear. That\u2019s what will be in Prometheus Unbound. No new specific powers for each dot of Mode, a system to let you make your own effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T19:21:22-07:00","id":1419281,"title":"","content":"That is quite exciting! Upon rereading your reply, it was clear. <br /> <br /> Some thoughts on Prometheus Unbound:<br /> --Every Psi Order getting attention means more on the Chitra Bhanu. My entire rpg group loves the approach of Onyx Path including the &quot;lost&quot; groups like Chitra or White Howlers in Werewolf. I much prefer an open sandbox as a storyteller. <br /> --This probably includes a detailed write up of each Proxy and other high-Psi psions within each order. Looking forward to see how they're built in Storypath. Access to higher Psi powers is another appealing tool to have included.<br /> --Bundling all the orders into a single book makes so much more sense than the old splat book format, both from sales and maximizing relevant word count. <br /> <br /> Another topic that has come out of group discussions on powers concerns telepathy, which this book may address. Can Telepaths link to other animals? If humans can link to aliens like Chromatics and Qin, why wouldn't we be able to communicate metaphorically (at least) with more intelligent animals like dolphins, octopi, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T22:56:28-07:00","id":1419310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419279#post1419279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I wasn\u2019t clear. That\u2019s what will be in Prometheus Unbound. No new specific powers for each dot of Mode, a system to let you make your own effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes...<br /> <br /> This is of great interest to me...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T23:29:23-07:00","id":1419314,"title":"","content":"The \u00c6on core already provides a fairly flexible system: each Mode allows you to do more than in 1e, plus you have the link-up effects from other psions to bolster your effects further.<br /> <br /> Just like Terra Firma was &quot;the countries of Earth from the core, plus a lot of additional off-the-wall stuff you didn't expect,&quot; and Distant Worlds was &quot;the colonies from the core, plus additional off-the-wall stuff you didn't expect,&quot; this will be the same thing for the psi orders. If you like the psi orders and you like the psi powers, you'll get that dialed up to 11 plus a lot of additional stuff you didn't expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T09:37:33-07:00","id":1419387,"title":"","content":"I admit that in PU I'm hoping to see stuff for Free-lance Psions and Psaids as well as stuff on the 8 Orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T11:10:27-07:00","id":1419400,"title":"","content":"Ian, I agree that the powers are more flexible from 1e; just inquiring about any plans for more options.<br /> <br /> Are there any plans to include rules for telepathy interacting with other species (aliens, other animals)? Maybe a difficulty chart that increases the more removed a species is from the telepath's thought type? I'm sure this is something I could wing as a Storyteller, but would value a chart for consistency.<br /> <br /> I haven't taken part in these forums in a looooooonnnnng time, but my group is ramping up for a return to Aeon after 15 years away from the setting. I ran a modern Talent game for 10 sessions to get us all acclimated to the core system and now we're salivating at the bolt-on rules for Psions and playing Aeon. <br /> <br /> Excellent job transitioning Trinity into its new Continuum!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T11:15:32-07:00","id":1419401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastion Avalos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419400#post1419400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans to include rules for telepathy interacting with other species (aliens, other animals)? Maybe a difficulty chart that increases the more removed a species is from the telepath's thought type? I'm sure this is something I could wing as a Storyteller, but would value a chart for consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 246 of TC:Aeon goes into this. There is a complication added based on how alien their minds are and how unwilling they are. Failure to buy off the complication means there's difficulty understanding each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T11:18:20-07:00","id":1419402,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Telepathy, I wouldn't mind seeing some kind of offensive use of telepathic powers described in P.U. Even if it's just giving people a &quot;sleep&quot; command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T14:20:06-07:00","id":1419434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419402#post1419402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Telepathy, I wouldn't mind seeing some kind of offensive use of telepathic powers described in P.U. Even if it's just giving people a &quot;sleep&quot; command.</div> </div> </div> </div>Command (Psychybending 2) can command to sleep, it\u2019s a minor effect when out of action, increase a bit if in combat, but yet possible.<br /> Exacerbate and Inflict Emotions (Rapport 2 and 4) can both be used to cause self damage. It\u2019s evil, but you can cause suicidal thoughts related to guilty and other feelings. Command can force a person to kill themself, or at least try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T16:06:43-07:00","id":1419471,"title":"","content":"I'm actually really looking forward to seeing how we can use the psi ratings for things that are related but slightly sideways to the actual modes in the book. <br /> <br /> Example being the potential for say an enemy psion to indoctrinate people using Telepathy or the ability of a TK to create say super materials by rearraging molecules and such. Plus other things. <br /> <br /> Also, while I know its going to focus on Psions I do hope there are some Psiad love - maybe some mention of how those with dots in multiple aptitudes and modes could combine effects. If they have to focus on the whole teamwork rules I am okay as long as they say &quot;this works if a psiad has both dots&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T17:01:35-07:00","id":1419483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419471#post1419471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example being the potential for say an enemy psion to indoctrinate people using Telepathy or the ability of a TK to create say super materials by rearraging molecules and such. Plus other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did get to write the best use <i>ever</i> for Selective Permeability.<br /> <br /> - C.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T17:41:45-07:00","id":1419488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tegyrius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419483#post1419483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did get to write the best use <i>ever</i> for Selective Permeability.<br /> <br /> - C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just hearing that such variant or specific uses for the powers is in the book makes me giddy. I don't even need to know what that is yet to be happy that such things are in the book. <br /> <br /> So yeah, awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T06:28:33-07:00","id":1419570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419434#post1419434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Command can force a person to kill themself, or at least try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didnt Command had a clause for no self-harm?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T07:33:01-07:00","id":1419579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419570#post1419570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didnt Command had a clause for no self-harm?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, not only on self harm, but also on breaking bounds. To make a person kill themself the Telepath needs to use Possession and cause all the damage while keep control over the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T10:35:50-07:00","id":1419606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419570#post1419570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didnt Command had a clause for no self-harm?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but figure that's for no obvious/direct self-harm - or harm to others for that matter. I remember something from Asimov's Robots novels with the three laws of robotics, one of which was &quot;No robot can harm a human or, through inaction allow a human to come to harm.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, one way around that would be to tell one robot to &quot;Pour this liquid in to that empty cup and then delete that action from your memory banks.&quot; The robot does this (and the liquid is a poison/allergen/otherwise deadly when consumed). Then you tell the robot &quot;Pour tea into the cup and then serve the cup Person X.&quot; Assuming Person X drinks the tea and dies, he robot has effectively (if unwittingly) helped to murder somebody despite the law.<br /> <br /> You could probably use Mind Control to similar effect. Like there's a gap between two areas with a 400 foot drop in normal gravity. A telepath could create the mental illusion of a sturdy, safe bridge across the gap, use Mind Control and tell somebody to walk across the bridge. At which point &quot;Ahhh&quot; *Splat*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 10-22-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T15:50:01-07:00","id":1419666,"title":"","content":"I remember the film Push, where one of the villains has one of his failed henchmen kill himself by psychic-pushing him to believe it's OK to obey the command to shoot himself in the head with a false memory of unloading his gun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T17:21:52-07:00","id":1419682,"title":"","content":"Push give a very good idea of how to deal with powerful telepathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T20:15:12-07:00","id":1419701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1419250-so-prometheus-unbound?p=1419606#post1419606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but figure that's for no obvious/direct self-harm - or harm to others for that matter. I remember something from Asimov's Robots novels with the three laws of robotics, one of which was &quot;No robot can harm a human or, through inaction allow a human to come to harm.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, one way around that would be to tell one robot to &quot;Pour this liquid in to that empty cup and then delete that action from your memory banks.&quot; The robot does this (and the liquid is a poison/allergen/otherwise deadly when consumed). Then you tell the robot &quot;Pour tea into the cup and then serve the cup Person X.&quot; Assuming Person X drinks the tea and dies, he robot has effectively (if unwittingly) helped to murder somebody despite the law.<br /> <br /> You could probably use Mind Control to similar effect. Like there's a gap between two areas with a 400 foot drop in normal gravity. A telepath could create the mental illusion of a sturdy, safe bridge across the gap, use Mind Control and tell somebody to walk across the bridge. At which point &quot;Ahhh&quot; *Splat*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yes, if you take a creative approach of course it ok. Its fun that way.<br /> <br /> You could also use a mental command to make someone do something stupid in the middle of a gun-fight and getting himself killed.<br /> <br /> You just cant spam Command Word: Kill and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T11:05:17-07:00","id":1419816,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of &quot;Shoot your friend&quot; and have been since 1e vampire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T11:14:13-07:00","id":1419818,"title":"","content":"Im more like, &quot;go pick up that bottle&quot; (and abandon cover in the process).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T20:16:40-07:00","id":1420204,"title":"","content":"I noticed that this book is listed as &quot;in development.&quot; Does that mean that the first and second drafts have been done?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T00:23:15-07:00","id":1420221,"title":"","content":"Yes, indeed. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T10:01:03-07:00","id":1420286,"title":"","content":"I kind of really hope its moved along the chain to us getting say a pdf release. Same with me hoping Terra Firma goes to pod soon, cause I watz it on my shelf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T11:16:03-07:00","id":1420296,"title":"","content":"Using Terra Firma as an example, it took 16 months from First Draft to the .pdf Advanced copy becoming available. <br /> 5/6/19- First showed up in First Draft on MMN<br /> 8/19/19- Moved to 2nd Draft (skipped Redlines)<br /> 10/7/19- Moved to Manuscript Approval stage<br /> 11/11/19- Moved to Editing <br /> 9/16/20 - release of the Advanced copy PDF<br /> <br /> Note that Terra Firma skipped Redlines, Development, and Post-Approval Development on the MMN. This doesn't mean they skipped them internally, but they weren't shown on the released status updates. <br /> <br /> Using that as the example, with Prometheus Unbound first arriving listed in First Draft stage on 7/13/20, that puts its PDF release in November 2021. There are obviously a lot of factors at play but from an outsider's perspective alone it appears we've got some waiting and enjoying of our currently-available content.<br /> <br /> Maybe we'll get pleasantly surprised and see it by next summer! In the meantime, we've still got Mission Statements and Under Alien Suns forthcoming to expand the Continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T11:18:38-07:00","id":1420297,"title":"","content":"What an interesting timeline of events. That said I hope it doesn't take to next year for us to get Prometheus Unbound, especially with how they have been talking about it. <br /> <br /> Of course, if it does, well, it is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 10-26-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T14:06:18-07:00","id":1420325,"title":"","content":"Redlines tend to be a pretty quick stage for books that aren't massive cores. Once the text is finalized, unless there's a reason for any major last-minute changes the big wait comes from contracting and acquiring the art (at least, to the best of my understanding of the process).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}